ef531e0f-dca4-405e-918c-3bf422e7ec6d,pilot.g4agent@syllabai-test.dev,b12213cd-082f-4c26-8ed4-56529f77c12a,sme-eq-1-3-atomic-structure-q10,sme-eq-1-3-atomic-structure-q10,b,4,"i) The species with six electrons in its outer shell is U. ii) The mass number of Z is 12 + 13 = 25. iii) The positive ion is W, because it has 11 protons but only 10 electrons. iv) The isotopes of the same element are W and X, because they have the same number of neutrons.",SMART_MARKED,,,,,,,4,"i) The letter of the species that has six electrons in its outer shell is:

